Subject: OpenVMS: environment variables without DCL symbols

The VSI C RTL's getenv() falls back to DCL symbols, and the command that
runs less is the symbol LESS :== $...LESS.EXE: getenv("LESS") returned
the image's file name, which less parsed as its options ("E" in "EXE"
made it quit at the end of the file).  On VMS lgetenv() uses
vms_getenv() (vms/vms_env.c): the C environment, then logical names,
never symbols (docs/DECISIONS.md D3).

--- a/decode.c	2026-09-09 02:42:36.000000000 +0100
+++ b/decode.c	2026-10-10 10:19:01.789521890 +0100
@@ -30,6 +30,9 @@
  */
 
 #include "less.h"
+#ifdef __VMS
+#include "vms_env.h"
+#endif
 #include "cmd.h"
 #include "lesskey.h"
 
@@ -1208,7 +1211,12 @@
 	if (!isnullenv(s))
 		return (s);
 #endif
+#ifdef __VMS
+	/* Not DCL symbols: LESS is the command's own (vms/vms_env.c). */
+	s = vms_getenv(var);
+#else
 	s = getenv(var);
+#endif
 	if (!isnullenv(s))
 	{
 #if !GETENV_NONVOLATILE
